  "title": "Circular photon orbits and the ISCO",
  "description": "Photon orbits: rays launched tangentially in the equatorial plane; bisection on the launch radius between falling in and escaping gives the circular photon orbit, compared with r = 2M (1 + cos(2/3 acos(-+a))). ISCO: from g and its derivatives evaluated on the GPU, circular geodesics have angular velocity Omega solving d_r g_tt + 2 Omega d_r g_tphi + Omega^2 d_r g_phiphi = 0; the ISCO is the minimum of their energy, compared with Bardeen, Press & Teukolsky (1972). Omega is also compared with the Boyer-Lindquist formula sqrt(M) / (r^1.5 + a sqrt(M)) that the disk model uses. Radii are Boyer-Lindquist (r^2 = x^2 - a^2 in the plane).",
